00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.060
Levels is a program that lets you see

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.950
how different foods affect your health

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.020
by giving you real-time
feedback on your diet

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.480
using a continuous glucose monitor.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.310
One of the most important features

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:22.560
of our immediate feelings of well-being

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.320
and our ability to focus and
think and move and have energy,

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.750
as well as our long-term health,

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.910
are our blood glucose levels.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.440
That is, our blood sugar levels.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.110
And that's because all the
cells and tissues of our body

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.030
and especially neurons, nerve cells,

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.400
rely on glucose for fuel.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.290
I realize some of you
out there are ketogenic,

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.790
and, yes, you can use ketones for fuel,

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:43.200
but the vast majority of people

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:46.590
are using glucose for fuel in their cells.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.840
If you want to maintain energy
and focus throughout the day,

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.450
you want to keep that blood glucose steady

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.230
and you don't want it ever
to spike or to drop too much,

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.790
so you need to understand
how different foods

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.320
and indeed how different activities

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.580
impact your blood glucose.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.530
I started using Levels about a year ago

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.530
as a way to understand how
different foods and exercise

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:06.930
and supplements and combinations
of food and exercise

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.520
and even sequencing, like when I do what,

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.170
how that affects my blood glucose levels.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.940
It's been tremendously informative.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.030
It's completely reshaped when
I exercise, how I exercise,

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.980
when I eat relative to
exercise, et cetera.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.810
So if you're interested in
learning more about Levels

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.180
and trying a continuous
glucose monitor yourself,

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.760
go to levels.link/huberman.

